<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sutri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sutri is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lazio">Lazio</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-cassia">Via Cassia</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, with an Etruscan past and a rock-cut amphitheatre. In 728 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> king Liutprand gave it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ii">Pope Gregory II</a>, the Donation of Sutri, regarded as the first territorial grant to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. In 1046 a synod held there deposed rival popes in the presence of Emperor Henry III.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sutri.jpg" alt="Sutri" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fiat 500e · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panorama_di_Sutri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
